# Build context exclusions for the Python image.
#
# The image is built from the repo root and does `COPY . .`, so anything not
# excluded here is baked into a layer -- permanently, even if a later layer
# deletes it. Two things matter: secrets must never enter the context, and
# host-built artefacts must never shadow what the image installs itself.

# --- Secrets. Never in an image, and never in a pushed layer. --------------
.env
.env.local
*.local

# --- Host-built artefacts ---------------------------------------------------
# Windows-built binaries that would break in the Linux container, and ~500MB
# of context that slows every build.
.venv/
venv/
node_modules/
.next/
out/
dist/
.turbo/

# --- Caches -----------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/

# --- Not needed at runtime --------------------------------------------------
.git/
.github/
docs/
.vscode/
.idea/
ForMe.txt

# --- OS ---------------------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
